{"assets":["/statement-assets/24fc5d8cde69c04a9a6824560240e65a2405a80cf17421a6c0bf91f5a2853458.png","/statement-assets/264dade177078b4af632a799a2d77b951c069703f61c7719f72fbbca211a005e.png","/statement-assets/fd900d129fd6a2260f0b29a640ed74243500207cfeceb243e99cc1bc6c6f015a.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1455","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Four Points"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given four different integer points $$$p_1$$$, $$$p_2$$$, $$$p_3$$$ and $$$p_4$$$ on $$$\\mathit{XY}$$$ grid."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In one step you can choose one of the points $$$p_i$$$ and move it in one of four directions by one. In other words, if you have chosen point $$$p_i = (x, y)$$$ you can move it to $$$(x, y + 1)$$$, $$$(x, y - 1)$$$, $$$(x + 1, y)$$$ or $$$(x - 1, y)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your goal to move points in such a way that they will form a square with sides parallel to $$$\\mathit{OX}$$$ and $$$\\mathit{OY}$$$ axes (a square with side $$$0$$$ is allowed)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"What is the minimum number of steps you need to make such a square?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test case consists of four lines. Each line contains two integers $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$ ($$$0 \\le x, y \\le 10^9$$$) — coordinates of one of the points $$$p_i = (x, y)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"All points are different in one test case."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print the single integer — the minimum number of steps to make a square."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n0 2\n4 2\n2 0\n2 4\n1 0\n2 0\n4 0\n6 0\n1 6\n2 2\n2 5\n4 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n8\n7\n5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, one of the optimal solutions is shown below: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/24fc5d8cde69c04a9a6824560240e65a2405a80cf17421a6c0bf91f5a2853458.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" Each point was moved two times, so the answer $$$2 + 2 + 2 + 2 = 8$$$."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, one of the optimal solutions is shown below: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/264dade177078b4af632a799a2d77b951c069703f61c7719f72fbbca211a005e.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" The answer is $$$3 + 1 + 0 + 3 = 7$$$."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, one of the optimal solutions is shown below: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/fd900d129fd6a2260f0b29a640ed74243500207cfeceb243e99cc1bc6c6f015a.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" The answer is $$$1 + 1 + 2 + 1 = 5$$$."}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1455E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1455/problem/E"}